5,"Tibetan Traditional Music: Folk Song, Sacred Chant, Heritage",https://tourtraveltibet.com/tibet/music/,"The Vibrant Tapestry of Tibetan Traditional Music Tibetan traditional music is an essential element of the region's cultural identity, offering a rich and diverse expression of its heritage. This dynamic art form encompasses multiple genres, including folk, religious, and court music, each playing a vital role in preserving and celebrating Tibet's unique traditions. Among these, Tibetan ...",Lunanakha,Sino-Tibetan
6,Tibetan Music Preservation | Traditional and Classical Music,https://tibetanmusicpreservation.wordpress.com/,"Tibetan Music Preservation (TMP) is an online initiative to preserve and promote endangered Tibetan traditional music. TMP projects include audio and video recordings of traditional and classical music, interviews of traditional artists. These online archives are free of charge for the public to access.",Lunanakha,Sino-Tibetan
7,"TIbetan Folk Songs, Tibetan Dance | NagmaToeshay, Lhu & more.",https://tipa.asia/study-and-training/folk-song-and-dance/,"If you want to know and learn about traditional Tibetan dance forms like NagmaToeshay and Lhu or Folk music, read about our courses here.",Lunanakha,Sino-Tibetan
8,"Tibetan Music: Traditions, Instruments & Cultural Roots",https://windhorsetour.com/tibet-culture/tibetan-music,"Explore the rich world of Tibetan music—sacred chants, folk songs, opera, and modern fusion. Discover key instruments, rituals, and cultural significance.",Lunanakha,Sino-Tibetan
9,Sino-Tibetan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/236/,"Lunanakha luk, a language of Bhutan · Sikkimese sip, a language of India · Western 3 · Jad jda, a language of India · Spiti Bhoti spt, a language of India · Stod Bhoti sbu, a language of India · Khams 1 · Tibetan, Khams khg, a language of China · Unclassified 1 ·",Lunanakha,Sino-Tibetan
